cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "HighRes-EERIE-NorthAtlantic-Evaluation: winter extremes, the NAO and high-resolution climate models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pradhan"
    given-names: "Himansu Kesari"
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/TunaHim/HighRes-EERIE-NorthAtlantic-Evaluation"
url: "https://tunahim.github.io/HighRes-EERIE-NorthAtlantic-Evaluation/"
abstract: >-
  An exploratory evaluation of North Atlantic winter circulation and European winter extremes
  in high-resolution climate models from the EU project EERIE, against ERA5 and E-OBS, in three
  experiments: which biases persist across three historical runs each of ICON-ESM-ER and
  IFS-FESOM2-SR; what internal variability alone can do in 29 winters, from 100-year control runs
  and atmosphere-only ensembles; and how circulation, the NAO and winter rain change across
  HadGEM3-GC5E coupled resolution configurations (about 135, 60 and 20 km) and IFS at 28 and 9 km.
  With a tested data pipeline, executed notebooks, a website, an interactive explorer and two posters.
keywords:
  - climate model evaluation
  - North Atlantic Oscillation
  - precipitation extremes
  - internal variability
  - model resolution
  - high-resolution climate models
  - EERIE
  - HadGEM3-GC5E
  - ERA5
  - E-OBS
  - north-west Europe
  - reproducible research
